/*  FUNCTION NAME:      COLOF
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Extracts the column number from an encoded position integer (as produced by TOPOS).*/
/*  RETURNS:            number: the column number; lifts over arrays
    PARAMETERS:
        pos             (Required) Encoded position (row*mult+col). Also accepts an array/range of positions — result lifts element-wise.
        mult            (Optional) Multiplier used during encoding. Default: the _mult constant (1000000, as TOPOS). Must match the mult used to encode pos.
    EXAMPLE:            =COLOF(17000017) -> 17
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-05-20  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-11-06  Claude      Default mult is the _mult constant (1000000), was a literal 100000 (#380)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
COLOF = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [pos],
    [mult],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        m, IF(ISOMITTED(mult), _mult, mult),
        result, MOD(pos, m),
        result
)
);
